SUMMARY:Kawartha Highlands Canoeing Trip
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Canoe Trippers\nJoin us for a weekend loop through Kaw
 artha Highlands Provincial Park!\n\n**Route**\nLong Lake Access Point → 
 Buzzard Lake (Site 424) → Triangle Lake (Site 530) → Long Lake Access 
 Point\n\n**When**\nMeet at the Long Lake Access Point at **10:00 AM on Fri
 day\, June 12**.\nWe'll head home on Sunday. Our final campsite is reserve
 d until **2:00 PM**\, in accordance with park rules.\n\n**Cost**\n**$22.00
  per person\, plus tax and parking.**\nParticipants are responsible for th
 eir own park fees. The reservation includes parking for one vehicle\, and 
 we'll split the cost of any additional vehicles among the group.\n\n**Port
 ages**\nThis route includes several portages\, so please pack accordingly:
 \n\n* 340 m\n* 685 m\n* 680 m\n* 990 m\n* 350 m\n* 1\,280 m\n\nIf you pref
 er to double-carry\, that's completely fine. Just keep in mind that it's b
 ug season\, so the quicker we can get across the portages\, the happier ev
 eryone will be. 😄\n\n**Trip Difficulty**\n**Intermediate.** Participant
 s should be comfortable paddling for a few hours each day\, carrying their
  own food and gear through multiple portages\, and being self-sufficient i
 n a backcountry setting.\n\n**Food & Gear**\nThis is a self-supported trip
 . Participants are responsible for bringing their own food\, canoeing equi
 pment\, camping gear\, and personal supplies for the weekend.\n\nComment b
 elow if you're interested in **carpooling**\, **sharing gear**\, or if you
  have any questions.\n\nLooking forward to another great weekend on the wa
 ter!
