DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260801T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260803T140000
SUMMARY:Car Camping + Flatwater Day Paddle at Algonquin\, Must join WCA me
 mbership $45
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Canoe Trippers\nThis is an event organized by Wilderne
 ss Canoe Association (WCA). Therefore\, you must join the membership to pa
 rticipate\, $45 for a single or $60 for a family.\n\nFor detail:\nhttps://
 wildernesscanoe.ca/content/join-wca\n\nInterested in introducing camping a
 nd flatwater canoeing to kids in your life?\nIt's my first time introducin
 g my 8 year old son to camping and canoeing and I'm looking for people in 
 a similar situation!\nI have space for 3-4 people on my trip as the maximu
 m capacity at a Ontario Parks car camping site is 6 people. I am a party o
 f 2.\nYou can rent the camping essentials + canoe at Algonquin Outfitters 
 so not to worry if you don't have any equipment.\nI booked 1 site at Rock 
 Lake campground and you are encouraged to book a site as well. Please reac
 h out to Susanna ([s_q_wong@yahoo.ca](mailto:s_q_wong@yahoo.ca)) for more 
 details.\n\nItinerary description\nItinerary is just a suggestion. There's
  no shuttles to catch and no firm schedule. Canoes are rented on a per day
  basis and Algonquin Outfitters does a great job at dropping off and picki
 ng up the canoes at either your campsite or at the canoe launch.\n\nSaturd
 ay Aug 1:\n5 pm - arrive at Rock Lake campsite. Set up camping equipment.\
 nI will try to arrive by 3 pm but I recognize that traffic will be busy as
  it is a long weekend.\n6 pm - group dinner. Prepare your meal at your lei
 sure. I have a camping stove you can use.\nNo plans after dinner.\n\nSunda
 y Aug 2:\na flexible day which can be filled with a paddle out on Rock Lak
 e. Rock Lake is a great destination to have a glimpse of an interior (back
 country) camping as there's backcountry sites on the same lake\, and depen
 ding on interest and paddling ability\, we can practice what a portage is 
 like.\n\nMonday Aug 3:\n2 pm - check out deadline for campsite. You may wi
 sh to leave earlier as traffic will be challenging.\nRequired Items to Bri
 ng\nTent\, sleeping gear\, your personal utensils and plates\, clothing\, 
 toiletries.\nSee note below on renting.\nFor those new to camping\, here i
 s a suggested list:\n[https://www.mec.ca/en/explore/camping-checklist](htt
 ps://www.mec.ca/en/explore/camping-checklist)\nfocus on the sections: kitc
 hen and cooking (your own utensils and plates)\, outdoor essentials\, clot
 hes and shoes\, personal stuff.\nI have a full kitchen set.\n\n**About ren
 tals:**\nyou can rent most of the items under: sleep and shelter\, campsit
 e set-up.\n[https://algonquinoutfitters.com/rental/camping-hiking/](https:
 //algonquinoutfitters.com/rental/camping-hiking/)\n\nI will be renting a c
 anoe from Algonquin Outfitters as I don't have my own boat.\n[https://algo
 nquinoutfitters.com/rental/canoes/](https://algonquinoutfitters.com/rental
 /canoes/)\n\nYou are free to bring your own canoe/kayak/SUP board.\nThe ca
 mpsite I booked does have electricity.\n\nTo register:\nsend an email to S
 usanna ([s_q_wong@yahoo.ca](mailto:s_q_wong@yahoo.ca))
